  {
    "@id": "https://fullcircle.ca/events/talking-circle-community-care/event_13650_0",
    "@type": [
      "http://schema.org/Event"
    ],
    "http://schema.org/url": [
      {
        "@id": "https://fullcircle.ca/events/talking-circle-community-care/"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/image": [
      {
        "@id": "https://fullcircle.ca/wp-content/uploads/2021/09/TalkingCircleImage-scaled-13.jpg"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom": [
      {
        "@id": "https://fullcircle.ca/events/talking-circle-community-care/"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Talking Circle: Community Care"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "<p><!-- wp:paragraph --></p><p>Artists: Kehewin Native Dance Theatre, Aria Evans, Carrielynn Victor, Jimmy Blais, Bruce Naokwegijig/ Debajehmujig</p><p><!-- /wp:paragraph --></p><p><!-- wp:paragraph --></p><p>Inviting all emerging Indigenous artists and those who support them: How can we ensure care and community support to new and emerging Indigenous artists? Other considerations include: How can emerging artists integrate self-care into their practice? What is the broader community&#8217;s responsibility to young artists so that they can be rooted in a healthy and healing community practice? What teachings and reciprocal actions do emerging artists need in order to ground themselves in these shifting seasons? This circle is open to Indigenous artists, mentors, teachers, and learners from all disciplines and practices.</p><p><!-- /wp:paragraph --></p><p><!-- wp:paragraph --></p><p>Preregister via Eventbrite at <a href='https://www.eventbrite.ca/e/talking-circle-community-care-tickets-151338626907' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener'>Talking Circle: Community Care</a></p><p><!-- /wp:paragraph --></p> "
      }
    ],
