    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "The spirits of Delta blues, ragtime, Howlin’ Wolf, and Django Reinhardt flow freely through this raw duo of A.W. Cardinal, an Albertan guitarist/vocalist who cut his teeth in the jazz clubs and crowded bar rooms of Montreal and New York, and one-woman rhythm section Jasmine Colette Ohlhauser on bass and percussion. Together, Blue Moon Marquee “plucks the danger from a Tom Waits melody, dances it a little further over the line with dark magic, teases the rhythms and raises a toast to back alley jazz.” (Canadian Music)"
