    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Nogojiwanong Indigenous Fringe Festival"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "<p><!-- wp:paragraph --></p><p><meta charset='utf-8'>Stories around a campfire, dance in the woods, songs under the night sky, standup comedy in a parking lot &#8211; the 2021 Nogojiwanong Indigenous Fringe Festival is bringing fabulous performing arts experiences into the fresh air on the Trent University campus in Nogojiwanong/Peterborough from June 21-27, 2021.</p><p><!-- /wp:paragraph --></p><p><!-- wp:paragraph --></p><p>Chosen by lottery as per Fringe tradition, this year six artists/groups will be coming to Nogojiwanong from other parts of Ontario. NIFF is glad to welcome back some of the artists who had planned to participate in the Covid-cancelled inaugural 2021 festival along with new applicants. All performances will be held outdoors with strict adherence to health protocols.</p><p><!-- /wp:paragraph --></p> "
      }
    ],
