  {
    "@id": "https://fullcircle.ca/events/tsf-push-industry-series/event_16434_0",
    "@type": [
      "http://schema.org/Event"
    ],
    "http://schema.org/url": [
      {
        "@id": "https://fullcircle.ca/events/tsf-push-industry-series/"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/image": [
      {
        "@id": "https://fullcircle.ca/wp-content/uploads/2022/01/P1844474-scaled.jpg"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom": [
      {
        "@id": "https://fullcircle.ca/events/tsf-push-industry-series/"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Indigenous Performing Arts  Practices: Artistic Processes - What we Carry (with Us)"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "<p><!-- wp:paragraph --></p><p><em>Facilitated by Lindsay Lachance<br />Panelists: Santee Smith,&nbsp;Tammy Hailiopua Baker, Tara Beagan<br />Witness: Deneh&#8217;Cho&nbsp;Thompson</em></p><p><!-- /wp:paragraph --></p><p><!-- wp:paragraph --></p><p><!-- /wp:paragraph --></p><p><!-- wp:paragraph --></p><p>Many Indigenous artists create and collaborate from places that are specific to who we are and where we come from. Languages, our territories, stories, values and lived experiences influence artistic process, and this session will explore how artists, educators, and designers infuse themselves into their practices. Our panelists will discuss how their family/nation/community- specific teachings, protocol, and knowledges are being transformed into their theatrical works.</p><p><!-- /wp:paragraph --></p><p><!-- wp:paragraph --></p><p>Please register at <a href='https://pushfestival.ca/industry/'>https://pushfestival.ca/industry/</a></p><p><!-- /wp:paragraph --></p> "
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/startDate": [
      {
        "@type": "http://schema.org/Date",
