    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@value": "&lt;p&gt;A Mile in Our Moccasins A short film created by Indigenous youth. It is the film’s purpose to combat HIV stigma and discrimination by giving insight into the realities and challenges faced by young people living with HIV.  A Mile in Our Moccasins was created by Lulu Gurney (Kincolith, BC); Martin Morberg (Whitehorse, Yukon); William Flett (Haida Gwaii); Preston Leon (Burns Lake, BC); Christina Tom (Prince George, BC) (20min) &nbsp; Journeys to [&hellip;]&lt;/p&gt;\\n"
      }
